    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0241" n="169" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg169"/>

                <head>Local Board of Health of Balsall Heath</head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Balsall Heath</placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1865-05-03">May 3, 1865</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Resolution passed at a meeting held by the Local Board
                        of Health of Balsall Heath</hi>.</p>
                <p>At a meeting of the Local Board of Health for the district of Balsall Heath, near
                    Birmingham, in the county of Warwick, held at their offices in Vincent street,
                    Balsall Heath, aforesaid, on Wednesday, the 3d day of May, 1865, it was</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Unanimously resolved</hi>, That this board desires to
                    express its deepest sympathy with the government of the United States of
                    America, and Mrs. Lincoln, in the bereavement which both have sustained by the
                    lamented death of the late President, and to record its horror and detestation
                    of the crime which has caused so great a national loss.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>SAMUEL BRIGGS,</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chairman</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
